  "transcription_table_base_caveat": "The Coq VM constants action_head_addr = 101, action_state_addr = 100, action_halt_addr = 102, tape_base_addr = 99, and fixture_table_base = 104 are pinned to the literal .nas labels tbase/state/head/halt/table at 99..104; rlink at 103 is reserved and unmodelled. check_minsky_nan16_step.py maps @head/@state/@halt/@tbase/@table to those symbolic names and compares mnemonic tuples; it does not check instruction encodings or the loader. The final theorem is a statement about the Coq VM model, not about the literal assembled NaN16 image.",
